# Python Port Plan — Step 12_context

## Goal

Port `week1_baseline/ruby/12_context` to `week1_baseline/python/12_context`.
This is the largest step yet — bigger than `10` or `11` combined. Three
threads, all real: (1) `Tasks::Base`/`Tasks::Player` removed entirely,
`Config` absorbs their responsibilities directly; (2) proper context-window
tracking with color-coded warnings and auto-compaction; (3) reasoning/
"thinking" content-block support added across all five backends, and
`Logger` loses its cost/provider/task tracking in exchange.

## Decisions made this session (2026-07-25)

| Question | Decision | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Mirror `Tasks::Base`/`Player` removal? | **Yes, delete `tasks/` entirely.** | Real, deliberate Ruby architecture change (confirmed: `Config` gained `system_prompt`/`model`/`provider_type`/`agent_max_*` directly; `Context`/`Agent`/`Logger` all lost their `task`/`task_settings` params symmetrically). Keeping `tasks/` in Python would carry an abstraction Ruby itself cut. No current functional loss — only `"player"` ever existed. |
| Mirror Logger's cost/provider/task-tracking removal? | **Yes, mirror it — but document prominently as a regression relative to `06`–`11`.** | Confirmed `Backends::Base` still fully defines `estimate_cost`/`usage_unit`/`usage_level` — nothing deleted from backends, just disconnected from Logger's call site. Same "declared but currently unused" pattern as `LoopError`/`quiet!`. Removal is symmetric and clean (Agent's calls and Logger's signature both dropped `task:`/`backend:` together) — deliberate, not half-finished. |
| `Agent#record_usage`'s dropped multi-provider usage-field fallback | **Fix in Ruby + Python.** Already fixed in Ruby (see below) — restores the `usageMetadata`/`prompt_eval_count`-style field lookup `06_the_logger` established, feeding it into `add_turn_tokens`/`update_tokens` instead of cost estimation. | Real bug: without it, `current_tokens` silently stays 0 for Gemini/Ollama, so `needs_compaction?` never trips no matter how full the real window gets. Not scope-narrowing — Agent has no other provider-specific logic; PromptBuilder/backends already normalize everything else. |

