### Backends — all five need reasoning-block support; `openai.py` needs a full rewrite

**Common contract** (documented in `backends/base.py`'s docstring, matching
Ruby's new comment block in `backends/base.rb`): every backend's
`parse_response` now returns content blocks that can include
`{"type": "reasoning", "text": ..., "signature": ..., "redacted": ...}`,
ordered first (before text/tool_use), matching each provider's native
ordering. `signature` is an opaque round-trip token consumers never
interpret.

- **`anthropic.py`**: `parse_response` maps native `"thinking"` blocks →
  `{"type": "reasoning", "text": block["thinking"], "signature": block["signature"]}`
  and `"redacted_thinking"` → `{"type": "reasoning", "text": "", "redacted": True, "signature": block["data"]}`;
  everything else passes through unchanged. New private `_assistant_content`/
  `_denormalize_block` inverse: reasoning blocks re-emit as native
  `thinking`/`redacted_thinking` (redacted → `{"type": "redacted_thinking", "data": signature}`,
  non-redacted → `{"type": "thinking", "thinking": text, "signature": signature}`).
  `to_messages` gains an `:assistant`-role branch calling this (previously
  assistant content passed through the generic `else` branch unchanged).
- **`gemini.py`**: `parse_response`'s `elif part.get("thought")` branch
  (checked *before* the existing `text` branch) → `{"type": "reasoning",
  "text": part.get("text", ""), "signature": part.get("thoughtSignature")}`.
  `to_payload` gains `"thinkingConfig"` in `generationConfig` — a private
  `_thinking_config()` returning `{"thinkingBudget": 0}` for the two
  current models, or `{"thinkingLevel": "LOW"}` for a
  `"gemini-3.1-pro-preview-customtools"` special case (commented out in
  `MODELS` right now — port the branch anyway, matching Ruby's own dead
  branch, since Ruby ships it despite the model being commented out of
  its own table). `_assistant_parts`'s inverse gains a `"reasoning"` case
  re-emitting `{"text": ..., "thought": True, "thoughtSignature": ...}`
  (signature only included if present). `tool_use` blocks also gain a
  `thoughtSignature` passthrough when present. MODELS table changes: only
  `gemini-3.5-flash`/`gemini-3.1-flash-lite` remain active (matches
  current Ruby — the third entry is commented out, port it as commented
  out too, don't silently drop the historical note).
- **`ollama.py`**: `to_payload` gains `"think": False`. `parse_response`
  gains a `content.append({"type": "reasoning", "text": message["thinking"]})`
  guard (only if `message.get("thinking")` is truthy/non-empty — Ruby:
  `message["thinking"] && !message["thinking"].empty?`, translate as
  `is not None and message["thinking"] != ""`, not a bare truthy check).
  MODELS table shrinks to just `"gemma4:e4b"` (confirmed — every other
  local-model entry `10`/`11` had is gone from `12`'s Ruby source; port
  the table as-is, don't restore the removed entries).
- **`ollama_cloud.py`**: same `think: false` + reasoning-block addition as
  `ollama.py`. MODELS table reordered/changed (`kimi-k2.5:cloud` before
  `minimax-m3:cloud` now, `gemma4:31b-cloud` added) — port the literal
  current table, not a merge with `11`'s.
- **`openai.py`**: **full rewrite**, not an incremental diff. Ruby's own
  comment explains why: gpt-5.x rejects `reasoning_effort` + tools on
  `/v1/chat/completions`, so this backend now targets the Responses API
  (`/v1/responses`) instead. New method shape: `to_input(messages)`
  (replaces `to_messages` — **not** the same name, no arity-fix precedent
  applies here since this is a structurally new method, not a regressed
  old one), `to_payload` builds `{model, instructions: context.system,
  input: to_input(...), tools, max_output_tokens, reasoning: {effort: "none"}}`,
  `parse_response` walks a `response["output"]` array (not
  `response["content"]`) handling `"reasoning"`/`"message"`/`"function_call"`
  item types, and a private `_assistant_items` inverse (text → one
  `{role: "assistant", content: text}` item if non-empty, tool_use blocks →
  `{"type": "function_call", "call_id", "name", "arguments": json.dumps(input)}`
  items; reasoning blocks are dropped when rebuilding — gpt-5.x doesn't
  need them echoed back at `reasoning.effort = "none"`). MODELS table is
  now `gpt-5.5`/`gpt-5.4-mini`/`gpt-5.4-nano` (fully replaces `10`/`11`'s
  table, don't merge). **Flag for `PromptBuilder#to_messages`'s direct
  delegator**: since `OpenAI` no longer defines `to_messages` at all,
  calling `PromptBuilder.to_messages()` against an OpenAI-backed builder
  would raise `AttributeError` — confirmed this is *also* true in Ruby
  (no `to_messages` method on the new `OpenAI` class either, would raise
  `NoMethodError`). Not exercised by any live code path (`Client`/`Agent`
  only ever call `to_api_payload`), so this is a **latent, pre-existing
  inconsistency in Ruby's own source**, not something introduced by the
  port — port faithfully (i.e. `PromptBuilder.to_messages()` stays a
  blind delegator, don't special-case OpenAI to paper over it), same
  "don't unilaterally resolve what the source hasn't" principle as the
  `register_tool` open question.

